.TH REDLINE 1 "2025" "redline 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redline \- a read-focused TUI code browser for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redline
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Redline is an emacs/helm/magit-flavored code browser that lives in a terminal
pane. It provides instant navigation (files, symbols, definitions, references,
grep), a git status/staging/commit surface, live file watching, and light
editing (commit messages, per-project notes).
.SH KEY BINDINGS
See the README.md for the full keymap cheat sheet. Common bindings:
.TP
\fBC-x C-f\fR Find a file in the project
.TP
\fBC-x g\fR Magit status (stage, unstage, commit)
.TP
\fBM-\fR.\fR Jump to the definition under point
.TP
\fBC-s\fR Incremental search forward
.TP
\fBM-x\fR Command palette
.TP
\fBC-x C-c\fR Quit
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-notes=plain\fR
On quit, print the annotation dump in the bare grep-addressable form
`path:line: text` (no header, no code lines, no orphan marker). The
default block form carries the orphan marker; see README.md.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/redline/config.toml
Configuration: theme, auto_reload, key-binding overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/redline/
Project registry, recents, and highlight cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit\fR(1), \fBemacs\fR(1)
.SH AUTHOR
Redline contributors.
